00:34:32.070 --> 00:34:37.770
Was there any thought process or backstory for Angela on this, or was this a total surprise?
关于安吉拉的这个设定有什么考量或背景故事吗，还是完全是个惊喜？

774
00:34:37.990 --> 00:34:39.250
No backstory for me.
我没什么背景故事。

775
00:34:39.250 --> 00:34:42.050
I think this made the writer's room chuckle, and it went in the script.
我想这让编剧室的人笑出了声，于是就写进剧本里了。

776
00:34:42.050 --> 00:34:47.710
Well, I feel very worried for Angela, knowing now that she hasn't had her sleep apnea machine for a while.
嗯，我真为安吉拉担心，现在知道她已经有一段时间没用睡眠呼吸暂停呼吸机了。

777
00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:48.590
I know.
我知道。

778
00:34:49.030 --> 00:34:50.910
This caused me to feel anxious.
这让我感到焦虑。

779
00:34:51.730 --> 00:34:58.390
I don't like thinking that people are without the necessary tools or medicines that they need for any period of time.
我不喜欢想到人们在任何一段时间内缺乏他们所需的必要工具或药物。

780
00:34:58.630 --> 00:35:00.170
You know what really bothers me?
你知道什么真的让我很困扰吗？

781
00:35:00.410 --> 00:35:00.770
What?
什么？

782
00:35:01.050 --> 00:35:07.250
It really bothers me if I'm watching a movie and someone gets even a minor injury and they don't deal with it immediately.
如果我在看电影时，有人受了伤，哪怕是轻伤，他们却不立即处理，这真的让我很困扰。

783
00:35:07.610 --> 00:35:08.210
It really...
这真的……

784
00:35:08.750 --> 00:35:09.070
I get...
我……

785
00:35:09.070 --> 00:35:10.610
I'm very distracted by it.
我会被这分散注意力。

786
00:35:10.610 --> 00:35:14.410
Like, someone gets a cut and they don't, like, wrap it up right.
比如，有人被割伤了，却不好好包扎。

787
00:35:14.650 --> 00:35:18.010
It happens a lot in action films, and it really bugs me.
动作片里经常出现这种情况，这真的很让我心烦。

788
00:35:18.150 --> 00:35:23.690
But what really bothers me is after someone gets an injury, when the villain presses on the injury.
但真正让我困扰的是，当某人受伤后，反派去按压他们的伤口。

789
00:35:24.190 --> 00:35:31.050
You know, like, someone gets, like, a bullet to the shoulder, and then when they're being interrogated by the villain, the villain presses on their wound.
你知道的，比如有人肩膀中弹了，然后当他们被反派审问时，反派会去按压他们的伤口。

790
00:35:31.230 --> 00:35:31.710
I can't...
我不能……

791
00:35:31.710 --> 00:35:34.110
It's the heebie-jeebies for me, and I can't deal with it.
这让我毛骨悚然，我受不了。

792
00:35:34.110 --> 00:35:42.090
But, well, do not watch the show alone, where they drop people off in the middle of nowhere, and they have to just survive, because they get injured,
那千万别看《荒野独居》这类节目，他们把人扔在荒郊野外，让他们自生自灭，因为他们会受伤，

793
00:35:42.310 --> 00:35:44.150
and they have to try to patch it up on their own.
而且他们必须尝试自己包扎伤口。

794
00:35:44.350 --> 00:35:44.710
No.
不。

795
00:35:44.830 --> 00:35:49.730
And if it gets really bad, they send a medic in, but it's got to get bad for the medic to, like, chop her in.
如果情况变得非常糟糕，他们会派一名医护人员进去，但必须得严重到一定程度，医护人员才会介入。

796
00:35:50.130 --> 00:35:50.410
No.
不。

797
00:35:50.590 --> 00:35:51.270
You couldn't do it.
你肯定做不到。

798
00:35:51.270 --> 00:35:51.830
See, I can't.
你看，我做不到。

799
00:35:51.950 --> 00:35:52.730
I couldn't do it.
我做不到。

800
00:35:52.730 --> 00:35:57.770
And then, you know, of course, you're constantly seeing, like, their banged-up thumb as they try to fish.
而且，你知道，你还会一直看到他们受伤的手指在试图钓鱼。

801
00:35:58.950 --> 00:36:00.230
Yeah, this is what I'm saying.
没错，我就是这个意思。

802
00:36:00.370 --> 00:36:00.770
I can't...
我不能……

803
00:36:00.770 --> 00:36:00.890
I can't.
我做不到。

804
00:36:00.930 --> 00:36:01.570
You can't do it.
你做不到的。

805
00:36:01.630 --> 00:36:02.270
You can't do it.
你做不到的。

806
00:36:02.350 --> 00:36:02.550
No.
不。

807
00:36:02.650 --> 00:36:09.470
Well, the last thing on the list, of course, is the chair figurine, and I want you guys to know, I own one.
好吧，清单上的最后一项当然是那个椅子摆件，我得让你们知道，我有一个。

808
00:36:09.830 --> 00:36:12.710
Do you have the one from the show?
你有剧里那个吗？

809
00:36:13.230 --> 00:36:13.590
No.
没有。

810
00:36:13.830 --> 00:36:14.190
No.
没有。

811
00:36:14.210 --> 00:36:15.450
It's so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

812
00:36:15.570 --> 00:36:16.730
I was given one as a gift.
我是别人送我的。

813
00:36:16.790 --> 00:36:21.810
I don't know when, even, like, in high school, from, like, I don't know, Aunt Brenda, did you give it to me?
我甚至不知道是什么时候，大概是高中吧，是布伦达阿姨送的吗？我不知道，是你给我的吗？

814
00:36:22.290 --> 00:36:30.690
Anyway, I have a little chair figurine, and it went with me to college and sat on my windowsill, and it made its way all the way to California.
总之，我有一个小椅子摆件，它陪我去了大学，放在我的窗台上，后来又一路跟着我到了加州。

815
00:36:31.190 --> 00:36:40.310
And it was on my dresser with, like, my dresser in the bedroom, and I need to go see if it's still there, because at some point, Isabel thought it was cute, and then Isabel would,
它原本放在我卧室的梳妆台上，我得去看看它还在不在，因为有段时间伊莎贝尔觉得它很可爱，然后伊莎贝尔就会，

816
00:36:40.410 --> 00:36:41.970
like, I think, put it in her room.
我想，把它拿到她的房间里去了。

817
00:36:42.230 --> 00:36:43.690
I'm going to try to track it down, guys.
伙计们，我打算去把它找出来。

818
00:36:43.890 --> 00:36:46.090
Anyway, long, boring story to tell you.
总之，讲了个又长又无聊的故事给你们听。

819
00:36:46.250 --> 00:36:48.470
In real life, I have a chair figurine.
在现实生活中，我确实有一个椅子摆件。

820
00:36:48.470 --> 00:36:55.330
Also, at 6 minutes and 24 seconds in this scene, Angela, you are wearing very high heels.
另外，这一幕在6分24秒的时候，安吉拉，你穿了非常高的高跟鞋。

821
00:36:55.590 --> 00:36:55.910
Why?
为什么？

822
00:36:56.150 --> 00:36:56.790
So high.
太高了。

823
00:36:57.070 --> 00:37:02.010
Oh, probably because I had to stand next to Rain, because normally in my scenes with him, he's seated.
哦，可能是因为我得站在雷恩旁边，因为通常我和他的对手戏里，他都是坐着的。

824
00:37:02.850 --> 00:37:09.490
And if I have to stand next to him, he's 6'3", I am 5'1", you get the big heels, get brought out.
如果我必须站在他旁边，他有6英尺3英寸（约1.9米），我只有5英尺1英寸（约1.55米），所以就得把大高跟鞋拿出来穿上。

825
00:37:09.890 --> 00:37:11.970
Well, these were massive.
好吧，这些鞋子太夸张了。

826
00:37:12.250 --> 00:37:13.070
Guys, check it out.
伙计们，快去看看。

827
00:37:13.230 --> 00:37:14.470
6 minutes, 24 seconds.
6分24秒。

828
00:37:14.470 --> 00:37:25.290
And also, if you toggle back to 6 minutes, 9 seconds, there's a great shot of my cat hair clip that Kim Ferry, who did my hair, made herself with, like, a glue gun.
还有，如果你切回到6分09秒，能清楚地看到我的猫咪发夹，那是负责我发型的金·费里用热熔胶枪亲手做的。

829
00:37:25.710 --> 00:37:30.310
And years later, she gave it to me in a shadow box, and I have my cat hair clips.
多年后，她把它装在展示盒里送给了我，现在我有我的猫咪发夹了。

830
00:37:30.630 --> 00:37:32.150
Aw, I know.
噢，我知道。

831
00:37:32.650 --> 00:37:40.690
So now we're going to move on to the scene where Kevin makes a big announcement to the bullpen that he would really love them to come see his band.
现在我们要进入凯文向办公室大厅宣布他非常希望大家去看他乐队演出的那一幕了。

832
00:37:40.890 --> 00:37:42.370
It's like a Battle of the Bands night.
那就像是一个乐队争霸赛之夜。

833
00:37:42.850 --> 00:37:47.870
And there's going to be an applause meter, and he will only win by clapping.
现场会有个掌声测量仪，他只能靠掌声取胜。

834
00:37:48.110 --> 00:37:51.950
And he wants everyone to come and clap for his band, Scrantonicity 2.
他希望大家都能去为他的乐队“斯克兰顿之音2号”鼓掌。

835
00:37:51.950 --> 00:37:55.650
Two, not Scrantonicity, which he is no longer a part of.
是2号，不是“斯克兰顿之音”，他已经不在那个乐队了。

836
00:37:55.890 --> 00:37:58.930
There is clearly some bad blood that we don't know about.
显然他们之间有些我们不知道的过节。

837
00:37:59.390 --> 00:38:02.970
But he invites the whole office to please come.
但他邀请了整个办公室的人去捧场。

838
00:38:03.910 --> 00:38:06.950
Well, we had a fan question about this.
好吧，我们收到了一个关于此事的粉丝提问。

839
00:38:07.230 --> 00:38:07.450
Okay.
好的。

840
00:38:08.110 --> 00:38:11.830
From Naomi Wye, Beatrice W., M.
来自娜奥米·怀、碧翠丝·W、M。

841
00:38:11.910 --> 00:38:15.210
Raines, Allison Quigley, and Elizabeth Shannon.
雷恩斯、艾莉森·奎格利和伊丽莎白·香农。

842
00:38:16.070 --> 00:38:17.110
They said,
她们问，

843
00:38:17.830 --> 00:38:20.550
Why didn't Pam go see Kevin's band?
为什么帕姆没去看凯文的乐队演出？

844
00:38:21.030 --> 00:38:24.130
No one came to her art show, and she felt so hurt.
没人去看她的艺术展，她当时感到非常受伤。

845
00:38:24.430 --> 00:38:29.170
Wouldn't she want to see Kevin so he wouldn't feel unsupported the way she did?
难道她不想去看看凯文，好让他不至于像她当时那样感到不被支持吗？

846
00:38:30.050 --> 00:38:30.650
Hmm.
嗯。

847
00:38:31.050 --> 00:38:33.030
Wow, that's a really good call.
哇，这问题问得真好。

848
00:38:33.450 --> 00:38:34.050
Yeah.
是啊。

849
00:38:34.290 --> 00:38:35.930
Here's what I'm thinking, guys.
伙计们，我是这么想的。

850
00:38:35.930 --> 00:38:39.230
I'm thinking, maybe she has gone to see his band.
我在想，也许她其实已经去看过他的乐队了。

851
00:38:39.470 --> 00:38:41.490
Maybe she went to go see Scrantonicity.
也许她去看Scrantonicity乐队的演出了。

852
00:38:41.810 --> 00:38:44.530
Maybe everyone in the office has gone to see it.
也许办公室里的所有人都去看演出了。

853
00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:48.270
And this is like another request to come see the band.
这就像是又一次邀请大家去看乐队演出。

854
00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:50.530
You know those people, right?
你知道那种人吧？

855
00:38:51.050 --> 00:38:53.850
Like, they're in the band, or they do stand-up.
就是那种玩乐队或者做单口喜剧的人。

856
00:38:53.970 --> 00:38:54.850
And you're like,
然后你就会说：

857
00:38:54.990 --> 00:38:57.450
Dude, I've seen seven of your stand-up shows.
老兄，你的单口喜剧我已经看过七场了。

858
00:38:57.590 --> 00:38:59.350
Like, I can't come to this one tonight.
今晚这场我实在去不了。

859
00:38:59.350 --> 00:39:00.690
I just can't do it.
我真的去不了。

860
00:39:01.490 --> 00:39:02.970
Maybe that's what's happening.
也许情况就是这样。

861
00:39:02.970 --> 00:39:06.930
I think I was this person, because I was always in an improv show.
我觉得我以前就是那种人，因为我总是在演即兴喜剧。

862
00:39:07.130 --> 00:39:07.590
I was always like,
我总是说：

863
00:39:07.690 --> 00:39:08.890
Hey, catch my improv show.
嘿，来看我的即兴表演吧。

864
00:39:09.090 --> 00:39:10.030
And people are like,
然后大家就说：

865
00:39:10.150 --> 00:39:13.450
You perform three times a week for like the last four years.
你过去四年里每周都演三次。

866
00:39:13.450 --> 00:39:15.690
I can't come see you do improv anymore.
我实在没法再去看你的即兴表演了。

867
00:39:16.030 --> 00:39:17.330
Stop asking me.
别再问我了。

868
00:39:17.730 --> 00:39:20.910
I can relate, too, because I did all that stuff, too.
我也深有同感，因为我以前也做过那些事。

869
00:39:21.070 --> 00:39:23.370
And I know that especially with stand-up,
而且我知道，尤其是做单口喜剧的时候，

870
00:39:24.070 --> 00:39:27.730
like, at least at the level that I was performing.
至少在我当时的表演水平下是这样。

871
00:39:27.770 --> 00:39:29.350
Guys, I didn't do stand-up.
伙计们，我没做过单口喜剧。

872
00:39:29.470 --> 00:39:32.830
I did this really weird comedic magic show.
我做的是一种非常奇怪的喜剧魔术表演。

873
00:39:32.830 --> 00:39:34.810
I won't go down that rabbit hole now.
我现在就不细说那段往事了。

874
00:39:35.270 --> 00:39:35.950
What?
什么？

875
00:39:36.250 --> 00:39:36.930
Yeah.
是的。

876
00:39:37.090 --> 00:39:37.470
What?
什么？

877
00:39:37.890 --> 00:39:38.830
I did.
我做过。

878
00:39:39.050 --> 00:39:40.650
It was like a...
那就像是……

879
00:39:40.650 --> 00:39:44.270
I was a silent comedic magician.
我是一个沉默的喜剧魔术师。

880
00:39:44.850 --> 00:39:45.210
What?
什么？

881
00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:49.410
And I performed to music in comedy clubs.
我在喜剧俱乐部里伴着音乐表演。

882
00:39:50.130 --> 00:39:53.090
Jenna, this is so amazing.
珍娜，这太神奇了。

883
00:39:53.370 --> 00:39:56.210
I cannot believe I didn't know this about you.
真不敢相信我竟然不知道你还有这一面。

884
00:39:56.350 --> 00:39:58.370
We've been friends for so long.
我们认识这么久了。

885
00:39:58.590 --> 00:40:00.950
You were like a comedic mime.
你就像个喜剧哑剧演员。

886
00:40:01.870 --> 00:40:02.410
Yeah.
没错。

887
00:40:02.570 --> 00:40:02.890
What?
什么？

888
00:40:03.210 --> 00:40:06.450
I would give anything to see that.
我愿意付出一切去看那场表演。

889
00:40:06.710 --> 00:40:07.170
Anything.
真的。

890
00:40:08.210 --> 00:40:12.610
I did magic tricks using my hands.
我用手变魔术。

891
00:40:12.810 --> 00:40:13.330
Oh, God.
天哪。

892
00:40:13.430 --> 00:40:14.630
And they weren't really magic.
而且那其实并不是真正的魔术。

893
00:40:14.630 --> 00:40:15.790
It was a joke.
那是个笑话。

894
00:40:15.970 --> 00:40:19.070
But I performed it as if I was a great magician.
但我表演的时候表现得好像我是一位伟大的魔术师。

895
00:40:19.070 --> 00:40:22.930
So, it was like an ironic kind of like...
所以，那是一种讽刺风格的……

896
00:40:22.930 --> 00:40:24.670
And you did it to music.
而且你是伴着音乐表演的。

897
00:40:24.890 --> 00:40:25.630
To music.
伴着音乐。

898
00:40:25.950 --> 00:40:26.950
And did you speak?
那你说话吗？

899
00:40:27.210 --> 00:40:27.650
No.
不。

900
00:40:27.970 --> 00:40:28.130
No.
不说话。

901
00:40:28.130 --> 00:40:29.090
There was no speaking.
当时没人说话。

902
00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:31.860
Yeah.
是啊。

903
00:40:31.860 --> 00:40:32.860
I need a photo.
我需要一张照片。

904
00:40:32.860 --> 00:40:33.660
I need a video.
我需要一段视频。

905
00:40:33.840 --> 00:40:34.620
I need something.
我需要点什么。

906
00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:35.460
Okay.
好吧。

907
00:40:35.540 --> 00:40:37.440
I'll do the show for you sometime.
改天我为你表演那个节目。

908
00:40:37.680 --> 00:40:40.640
This was my only foray into...
那是我唯一一次尝试……

909
00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:41.820
What?
什么？

910
00:40:42.300 --> 00:40:46.420
Promise me we will have wine together and you will do this for me.
答应我，我们要一起喝红酒，而且你要为我表演那个。

911
00:40:46.540 --> 00:40:46.800
Promise me.
答应我。

912
00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:47.400
I'll do it.
我会做的。

913
00:40:47.400 --> 00:40:49.980
I still have my tuxedo and the music.
我的燕尾服和配乐还在呢。

914
00:40:50.560 --> 00:40:50.980
Yeah.
是啊。

915
00:40:51.140 --> 00:40:51.760
I still have it.
我全都留着呢。

916
00:40:51.960 --> 00:40:52.920
You wore a tuxedo.
你穿过燕尾服啊。

917
00:40:53.180 --> 00:40:53.740
Yes.
是的。

918
00:40:53.740 --> 00:40:55.380
I was a fancy magician.
我以前是个时髦的魔术师。

919
00:40:55.560 --> 00:40:57.200
I wore a coat and tails.
我穿过那种带燕尾的礼服。

920
00:40:57.660 --> 00:40:58.660
Oh, my God.
天哪。

921
00:40:59.200 --> 00:40:59.460
Yeah.
是啊。

922
00:40:59.800 --> 00:41:00.680
So, listen.
所以，听着。

923
00:41:01.460 --> 00:41:03.060
My point is...
我的意思是……

924
00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:05.200
I don't know how to come back from that.
我不知道该怎么接这个话茬。

925
00:41:05.320 --> 00:41:05.760
I don't know.
我不知道。

926
00:41:05.840 --> 00:41:07.000
It's going to take me a beat.
我得缓一缓。

927
00:41:07.300 --> 00:41:07.780
Okay.
好吧。

928
00:41:07.780 --> 00:41:08.600
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

929
00:41:08.600 --> 00:41:14.860
What I'm saying in relation to Scranton City 2 is in my experience performing this show,
